If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not abruptly discontinue an opioid.
If a patient receives a high-dosage-opioid and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not abruptly discontinue an opioid especially for the patient.
If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not dismiss a patient from a care.
If a patient has a pain then every clinician should ensure an appropriate-pain-care for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-complication then every clinician should ensure an appropriate-opioid-use-complication-care for the patient.
An opioid-use-complication-example is an opioid-use-disorder-example.
